🕌Aladdin East Club

The Aladdin East Club is a student organization of the Faculty of International Economic Relations that brings together everyone interested in the culture, history, languages, and contemporary development of Eastern countries. We provide a welcoming environment for communication, personal growth, and exploring the rich traditions and cultural heritage of the Middle East, Central Asia, and East Asia.

📅 Events & Recruitment

Throughout the academic year, the club organizes:

— lectures and guest speaker sessions;
— Eastern language speaking clubs;
— workshops;
— quizzes and interactive cultural games;
— museum and exhibition visits;
— cultural events open to both Financial University students and anyone interested in Eastern cultures.

Announcements about recruitment of new members and the dates of upcoming events is posted on the club’s official information channels.

👥 Contact Information for Club Leaders

